{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-18251-r4494292","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Zelenchukova Supa (Bulgarian Vegetable Soup)","sourcePageId":18251,"sourceRevision":"4494292","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-05-25T21:04:23Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Zelenchukova%20Supa%20(Bulgarian%20Vegetable%20Soup)&oldid=4494292","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:42:46.279Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Boiled recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using beet","Category:Recipes using bell pepper","Category:Recipes using cabbage","Category:Recipes using carrot","Category:Recipes using celery","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using onion","Category:Recipes using paprika","Category:Recipes using parsley","Category:Recipes using potato","Category:Recipes using sunflower oil","Category:Recipes using tomato","Category:Recipes using wheat flour","Category:Recipes using yogurt","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Russian recipes","Category:Soup recipes","Category:Vegetarian recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"e40d9564972484cb678f8509b71f376d3fa460fd4bfee5a1a5b4c742ff8b4e1f","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Soup recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\n== Ingredients ==\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]]\n* 1–2 [[Cookbook:Carrot|carrots]], [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]]\n* ½ ea. [[Cookbook:Celery|celery]], diced\n* 1–2 [[Cookbook:Bell Pepper|bell peppers]], finely cut\n* ¼ of a medium-sized [[Cookbook:Cabbage|cabbage]], finely cut\n* 2–3 [[Cookbook:Potato|potatoes]], diced\n* [[Cookbook:Sunflower Oil|Sunflower oil]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], finely [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* 2–3 [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomatoes]], [[Cookbook:Grater|grated]]\n* 1 spoonful [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n* 1 tsp [[Cookbook:Paprika|paprika]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Beetroot|beetroot]], diced and [[Cookbook:Boiling|boiled]]\n* 100 g [[Cookbook:Yoghurt|yogurt]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]]\n* [[Cookbook:Parsley|Parsley]], finely chopped\n* 100 g [[Cookbook:Kashkaval|kashkaval]] (yellow cheese)\n\n== Procedure ==\n# Bring a pot of salted water to a [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]], then add the carrots, celery, peppers, and cabbage. Cook until soft. \n# Add the diced potatoes.\n# Heat some oil in a [[Cookbook:Frying Pan|pan]], and add the onion. Cook until soft, then stir in the flour, paprika, and tomatoes. \n# Stir the onion mixture into the boiling vegetables, and cook for another half hour.\n# Add the beetroot.\n# Combine the yogurt and egg, carefully mix in a bit of hot broth, then stir this mixture back into the soup to thicken it.\n# Season with salt to taste.\n# Serve with finely chopped parsley and grated kashkval.\n\n[[Category:Soup recipes]]\n[[Category:Russian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes_with_metric_units]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using carrot]]\n[[Category:Recipes using celery]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bell pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using potato]]\n[[Category:Recipes using onion]]\n[[Category:Recipes using tomato]]\n[[Category:Recipes using paprika]]\n[[Category:Recipes usin